  "caption": "Quinn found a squishy lump behind the knee, named it Gary, and noticed full bends felt tight.\n\nA lump like this is often a Baker's cyst: extra fluid from an irritated knee pushing into a pouch at the back. It's usually a sign of what's happening inside the knee, so the knee is the main focus.\n\nWhat often helps: an exercise and load plan for the knee, easing load with gentle compression and elevation during flares, keeping range and thigh strength, and shortening the range if deep bends are sore.\n\nSudden calf pain, swelling, warmth or redness needs same-day medical assessment, even if you already know about a cyst. If a child has one, a GP check is a sensible start.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
